Subject: secr 4.6.4
Message-ID: <DGuxjzC7LM8.eFcf275FAwAJ@secrgroup.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/secrgroup/c/DGuxjzC7LM8/m/eFcf275FAwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

secr 4.6.4 is now on CRAN. This version adds some simulation options e.g., the log-gaussian Cox distribution of activity centres (via the 'rLGCP' function of spatstat that in turn requires the non-CRAN package RandomFields -- see ?sim.popn). Multi-session data may now be fitted with  parameters for the initial density and session-on-session rate of increase (lambda) (see secr-trend.pdf <https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/pdfs/secr-trend.pdf>). Other minor changes are listed in NEWS. <https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/secr%204.6.4%20NEWS.txt>

